# Copy to .env for local development. Production values are set in the
# Cloudflare Pages dashboard under Settings > Environment variables.
#
# This site is built by Cloudflare Pages directly from the Git integration
# (there is no deploy workflow in .github/workflows), so dashboard variables
# ARE visible to the build. That is not true of every project — where the
# build runs in GitHub Actions instead, a dashboard variable is invisible to
# the bundle and has to be set on the build step in the workflow.

# ── Analytics consent ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set to 1 to require consent before the Zaraz GA4 tool is allowed to load.
# When enabled, an unanswered banner counts as a decline, and the choice is
# recorded in the `analytics-consent` cookie.
#
# Astro inlines PUBLIC_ prefixed variables into the client bundle at BUILD
# time. Changing this value in the dashboard does nothing until a new build
# runs — retry the latest Production deployment, or push to main.
#
# The PUBLIC_ prefix is required. Astro will not expose an unprefixed
# variable to client code, so `ANALYTICS_REQUIRE_CONSENT` (no prefix) reads
# as undefined in the browser and the consent banner silently never appears.
# There is no server-side code in this repo, so the unprefixed form has no
# use here at all.
PUBLIC_ANALYTICS_REQUIRE_CONSENT=1
